# Live and PACKS are one fabric

Read `docs/PACK-FACTORY.md` and `docs/ROUTING-FREEZE-2026-09-03.md` before
building or publishing a region. Cursor's Pack Factory skill is an execution aid;
the checked-in repository contract wins on conflict.

Each promoted V3 region uses the same R2 objects for LIVE and phone downloads:

- `dirt-packs/{id}/graph.v3.bin`
- `dirt-packs/{id}/geometry.v1.bin`
- `dirt-packs/{id}/fuel.v1.json`

Regions not yet promoted to V3 may advertise `graph.v2.bin` until their factory
run is accepted. The two checked-in V3 registries determine which graph LIVE and
the clients request.

- Foundational regional packs are OSM-only.
- Downloaded versus cellular is delivery, not a second road network.
- If a pack changes, publish it through an immutable candidate and promotion or
  it was not tested.
- Vercel contains API code only. Never include pack binaries or
  `longhaul.v1.json.gz` in the deployment.
- The accepted NS/NB/PE/NL/QC/ON V3 bytes are frozen reference moulds. Do not
  rebuild them while producing another region.

## When you change routing or packs

| Change | Required release action |
| --- | --- |
| New/rebuilt region | Follow `docs/PACK-FACTORY.md`: build graph/geometry/fuel, upload `--candidate --pack`, add both V3 registries and commit, deploy the recorded candidate override, accept, `--promote --pack`, `--live`, then region-scoped `--assert`. |
| Cost, access, or search law | This reopens the frozen routing candidate. Update Swift and JS twins, add a fixed regression, commit, deploy LIVE, install a new app build, and obtain physical acceptance before a new freeze. |
| Live loader only | Edit the shared pack-fabric source, commit, deploy LIVE, and assert every explicitly affected region. |

No routing or pack change is shipped when it exists only on the phone, only on
LIVE, or only on the laptop.

## Forbidden

- Bare `--pack` publication.
- Replacing the remote catalog with the checked-in seed manifest.
- Auto-downloading packs merely to make LIVE match.
- Longhaul or a second live extract.
- Provincial supplements in a foundational OSM-only build.
- A router-cost/search change hidden inside Pack Factory.
- Bulk promotion without region-by-region acceptance and identity evidence.

## Guarded commands

```sh
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --candidate <release-id> --pack <region>
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --candidate <release-id> <region> --live
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --promote <release-id> --pack <region>
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --live
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --assert --region <region>
```

